<Prose
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What data this site does and does not collect. Your PDF files are processed on your device and never uploaded."
  h1="Privacy Policy"
>
  <p>Last updated: 21 July 2026</p>

  <h2>Your files</h2>
  <p>
    PDF files you use with the tools on this site are processed entirely on your device, in
    your browser. They are never uploaded, transmitted, stored, or seen by us or by any
    third party. This is not a policy choice that could quietly change — the site has no
    server capable of receiving files, and the open-source code can be inspected to verify
    it.
  </p>
  <div class="prose-accent">
    <p class="mb-2">Verify it yourself:</p>
    <p class="text-sm">
      Open your browser's DevTools → Network tab while converting a file. You will see zero
      requests carrying file data.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to understand aggregate traffic (page views, country,
    browser type). It is cookie-free and does not track you across sites. We see counts,
    not people.
  </p>

  <h2>Error reporting</h2>
  <p>
    If a tool crashes, a technical error report (error type and stack trace) may be sent to
    our error-tracking service. These reports never include your files, file names, file
    contents, or any page data.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    The site may show ads to cover its costs. If Google AdSense is enabled, Google may use
    cookies as described in its own policies, and you will be asked for consent where the
    law requires it. Ads never appear inside the tool working area, and ad scripts have no
    access to your files.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Because we do not collect personal data about you, there is normally nothing for us to
    access, correct, or delete. If you believe otherwise, or have any privacy question,
    contact us — see the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</Prose>
